\emph{Proof sketch.}
For confounding and mediation, a Frisch--Waugh--Lovell decomposition shows the bias is $B(C) = R(C)/D(C)$, where $D(C)>0$ and $|R(C)|$ is bounded by the Cauchy--Schwarz inequality. The bound ensures $|B(C)| < |\tau|$ whenever the true effect and the omitted-variable (or total) effect share the same sign, guaranteeing sign preservation for all column-stochastic $C$.

